From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 23:29:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04559/11362] [outer-loop] GAP-4891 BREAKTHROUGH: relational
 target-match goal-energy SEPARATES on 3/4 stalled games

The count->scalar->relational ladder's first POSITIVE. Built induce_goal_energy_relational
(arc_agi3_goal_induction.py): translational self-similarity with a background-excluded induced
mask -- find the offset where the win's non-bg content matches its own translate (canvas ==
target-shown-at-offset), mask = that match-set, energy = mask-cells where g != g-shifted (0 at
the win, >0 at near-win negatives). This defeats the near-win-frame problem that killed every
global scalar. 3 unit tests (10 total) pass.

EMPIRICAL on the 4 grid-based stalled games (adversarial_verify clean 4/4):
  cd82 SEPARATES (winE=0, mean-nonE=12.8, frac_nonwin_above_max_win=1.0)
  sk48 SEPARATES (winE=0, nonE=29.0)
  sp80 SEPARATES (winE=0, nonE=3.27)
  cn04 FAILS  (alignment -- count+scalar+relational all fail -> learned/masked predicate)

So the GAP-4891 goal-ENERGY representation gap is CLOSED for 3 of 4: the energy is 0 on the win
and >0 on EVERY non-win incl. the near-win frame -- where counts (GAP-4890) and richer scalars
both returned None. The operator drops into the graph_explore_solve_v2 goal_energy hook + is
live-path-eligible.

HONEST RESIDUALS (separation is necessary, not sufficient): (1) stage-2 -- confirm the energy
GUIDES the search to a reproduction-gated L3, not just orders the frontier; (2) cn04 alignment
needs a relational predicate beyond translation. GAP-4891 status -> building (3/4 closed).

